# GLM-5.3-Flash-X ΓÇö findings by GPT 6.1 Sol- Source: Z.ai / Zhipu AI; spelling audit of queued `glm-5.3-flash-x` against published `glm-5.3-flashx`.- Date: 2026-10-22 (UTC)- Overview and scoring methodology: [model-comparison](../../model-comparison.md)- Cross-model signed log: [model-findings](../../model-findings.md)- Status: **Self-excluded: real FlashX access/specifications verified, but no exact task-quality benchmarks sufficient for Overall.**## Model card- **Name:** Dataset label GLM-5.3-Flash-X; verified publisher spelling **GLM-5.3-FlashX**.- **Identity:** Local `meta.json` is explicitly `scaffolded: true`, proposing `opencode/glm-5.3-flash-x` with generic 128K/text/standard-pricing fields. Those are not evidence of a second model. Publisher docs instead name `glm-5.3-flashx`, also independently present as `z-ai/glm-5.3-flashx` on OpenRouter.[1][2] The extra-hyphen folder is a likely spelling duplicate of already tracked `glm-5.3-flashx`; no separate checkpoint was established for `flash-x`. This report records the ambiguity without merging permanent folders.- **Provider / access / IDs:** Native model code `glm-5.3-flashx`, Chat Completions; OpenRouter **`z-ai/glm-5.3-flashx-20260918`**, Z.AI FP8 endpoint, `status: 0` and advertised 100% recent uptime at inspection.[1][2] These are catalog observations, not an authenticated inference test. Zen's live catalog lists `glm-5.3-flash` and `glm-5.3-flash-free`, not FlashX or Flash-X.[3]- **Release / knowledge:** Gateway backend points to **2026-09-18**; CometAPI also dates launch September 18. No exact knowledge cutoff verified.[2][4]- **Context window:** Publisher **1M / 128K output**; inspected gateway **1,048,576 / 131,072**. These are serving limits, not retention measurements.[1][2]- **Modalities / controls:** Native image/video/text/file input, text output, tool calling and structured output. Native thinking is mandatory; publisher recommends `reasoning_effort: max`, `temperature: 1`, `top_p: 0.95`. The inspected gateway supports `tool_choice: auto`, but reports forced/required/none selections unsupported; generic function-call support does not imply every selection mode.[1][2]- **Pricing (2026-10-22):** Native **$0.37 input / $1.25 output / $0.075 cached input per 1M tokens**; cache storage temporarily free. Inspected gateway **$0.37/$1.25/$0.09 cached**. Free cache storage is not free inference. No exact current zero-price FlashX route verified; publisher says FlashX is not yet in the GLM Coding Plan.[1][2][5]- **Architecture / relationship:** Publisher groups Flash/FlashX together and describes Flash's 320B-total/18B-active hybrid sparse/linear-attention base. OpenRouter calls FlashX the high-speed variant; models.dev maps it to base canonical `zhipuai/glm-5.3-flash`.[1][2][6] This supports a serving-tier interpretation, not an independently verified new quality checkpoint. No distinct FlashX weights/license artifact was verified.- **Legal variant boundary:** `glm-5.3-flashx-legal` is explicitly specialized with legal-domain mid/post-training. Its scores are not general FlashX scores.[1]### Raw benchmarks found- **Agent / tool use:** no verified public score found for exact Flash-X or FlashX task success on Terminal-Bench, Tau-bench, GDPval-AA, MCP-Atlas, or Claw evaluations.- **Reasoning / knowledge:** no verified public score found for an exact FlashX GPQA, HLE, CritPt, or Intelligence Index run.- **Coding:** no verified public score found for an exact FlashX SWE-bench, LiveCodeBench, SciCode, DeepSWE, or Vibe run.- **Long context / perception:** no verified public score found for exact FlashX retrieval, image/video task accuracy, or full-window retention.- **Real serving evidence:** Publisher advertises **200 tokens/s** for FlashX, without a verified standardized workload, TTFT distribution, or independent exact-route throughput run. This is a throughput claim, not a quality benchmark. Gateway runtime fields were null at inspection.[1][2]- **Why the shared documentation is insufficient:** Its numerical Intelligence Index, DeepSWE, AutomationBench, and coding charts explicitly label **GLM-5.3-Flash**, not a separately measured FlashX route. The legal appendix explicitly labels the legally trained variant. Neither set is imported into this entry's quality scores.[1]- **External cross-check:** CometAPI explicitly says published intelligence results belong to base Flash and no separate FlashX task-quality suite was published at launch. Its article's very high monetary figures conflict with the primary live tariff, so those article prices are not used.[4][5] The guessed exact AA, BenchLM, and Vals profiles returned HTTP 404; these bounded path failures do not establish global absence.[7][8][9]### Normalized scores (1ΓÇô100)Withheld. Verified identity clues, limits, tariff, and a vendor speed claim do not supply the missing quality-axis task measurements needed for Overall. No placeholder numbers or unlabelled base/Legal benchmark transfers are assigned.### Fresh search trail and sources- Bing RSS [`"GLM-5.3-Flash-X" benchmark`](https://www.bing.com/search?format=rss&q=%22GLM-5.3-Flash-X%22+benchmark): unrelated LinkedIn/airline results.- Google [`"GLM-5.3-FlashX" Z.ai`](https://www.google.com/search?q=%22GLM-5.3-FlashX%22+Z.ai): JavaScript/access interstitial.- DuckDuckGo [`"GLM-5.3-FlashX" benchmark`](https://duckduckgo.com/html/?q=%22GLM-5.3-FlashX%22+benchmark): CometAPI article found and inspected. Separate [`"GLM-5.3-Flash-X" "benchmark"`](https://duckduckgo.com/html/?q=%22GLM-5.3-Flash-X%22+%22benchmark%22): no results. The guessed native `/glm-5.3-flashx` page 404s; the actual shared `/glm-5.3-flash` page resolves and documents FlashX.[1][1]: https://docs.z.ai/guides/llm/glm-5.3-flash[2]: https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/models/z-ai/glm-5.3-flashx/endpoints[3]: https://opencode.ai/zen/v1/models[4]: https://www.cometapi.com/what-is-glm-5-3-flashx/[5]: https://docs.z.ai/guides/overview/pricing[6]: https://models.dev/api.json